                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7114d4f1-7801-4757-ac5d-a9479067f845",
                                "sense_id": "670b3118-610c-3e52-bcad-043245252357",
                                "text": "Maybe you had to have grown up in that nervous decade, as Mr. Weber did, to find Mr. Baker’s ostentatious laid-backness subversive, to imbue it with so much bad-boy allure. Mr. Weber, who is also a fashion photographer, is a glamorizer both by trade and by nature, and when something imprints itself as strongly on his fantasy life as the image of the young Chet Baker clearly did, he holds onto it tightly — cherishes it, embellishes it, uses it to transport himself back to his own hard-dreaming youth."
                            }
                        ]
